Function 1: Implement a command to open and read a file, and execute the command to read the contents of the specified file into a data structure established by itself in memory.
    Example: 1 data.txt
Function 2: Output a specified range of lines on the screen, and execute this command to display certain lines of the text file that have been read into memory on the screen.
Function 3: Line Insertion, execute this command to insert a line at a specified location.
Function 4: Line Delete, execute the command to delete one line or several consecutive lines.
Function 5: Inline text insertion, execute this command to insert one or more characters at a certain character in a certain line.
Function 6: Inline text deletion, run this command to delete several characters at a certain character in a certain line.
Function 7: Text Lookup, run this command to find the location of the first occurrence of a string starting from the specified line.
Function 8: Save the text file, run this command to write the modified text content to a new file.
Function 9: quit
Function 10: clear
Function 11: show Menu